body:
Makes sense, but needs a squash. At a minimum this restores the intention of the original code. Side note: This is why I prefer to use names like `name_index` in my own code, so I would personally change this to:

```cpp
for (int name_index = 0; name_index < names.size(); name_index++) {
	path_string += "/" + names[name_index].operator String();
}
```

EDIT: Or the `for (const StringName &name : names) {` style is even better.
